{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The Bluetooth USB adapter feels like a natural next choice because my WiFi and Ethernet adapters show an interest in adding useful connection options to my computer, provided it supports my operating system.",
    "The USB card reader and wired earbuds connect with my past USB accessories and headset purchase, so they fit some of my interests even though I do not need them now."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The hard drive, memory kits and graphics card assume I want to upgrade computer components, while my purchases reflect specific accessory and connection needs rather than a planned rebuild.",
    "The smart speaker and powered duster do not solve a current problem for me, and the earbuds, card reader and memory card offer little reason to act while my existing equipment is sufficient or I have no task requiring them."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "Buying desktop accessories seems to have been treated as interest in almost any desktop hardware, even components requiring a separate upgrade decision.",
    "Having bought a headset or USB accessory seems to have been taken as a reason to suggest more related products without considering whether they add a useful capability."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My purchases are spread far apart and address particular practical needs; I rarely choose something just because it relates to equipment I own.",
    "Compatibility and a clear use matter to me: the Bluetooth adapter could add a connection option, whereas memory needs a confirmed device match and removable storage needs an actual task."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly recognized my interest in practical computer connections but stretched that into broader hardware interest without enough attention to immediate need and compatibility."
}"}
